    "headline": "Lake Wind Advisory issued November 3 at 2:24AM PST until November 3 at 4:00PM PST by NWS Reno NV",
    "description": "* CHANGES...No changes.\n\n* WHAT...Southwest winds 15 to 20 mph with gusts up to 30 mph and\nwaves 1 to 3 feet, highest from mid-lake to eastern shores.\n\n* WHERE...Greater Lake Tahoe Area.\n\n* WHEN...From 9 AM this morning to 4 PM PST this afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...Strong winds and rough waves on area lakes will create\nhazardous conditions for small craft.",
    "instruction": "Check lake conditions before heading out and be prepared for a sudden\nincrease in winds and wave heights. Consider postponing boating\nactivities on the lake until a day with less wind.",
